  "nl_text": "The database schema named rschema_0438 consists of six tables.\nThe User table is used to store user information. It includes columns for Contact_Information, Password, Registration_Time, User_ID, and Username. The User_ID is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity as no two users can have the same ID.\nThe Product table stores product information. It includes columns for Price, Product_Description, Product_ID, Product_Name, and Stock_Quantity. The Product_ID is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity for each product.\nThe Add_to_Cart table is used to store information about which products a user has added to their cart. It includes columns for Is_Selected, Product_ID, Quantity, and User_ID. The combination of User_ID and Product_ID forms the primary key, ensuring entity integrity. The Product_ID and User_ID are foreign keys referencing the Product and User tables respectively.\nThe Order table stores information about user orders. It includes columns for Order_ID, Order_Status, Order_Time, Product_ID, Quantity, Total_Price, and User_ID. The Order_ID is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity for each order. The Product_ID and User_ID are foreign keys referencing the Product and User tables respectively.\nThe User_and_Order table is a junction table that links users and orders. It includes columns for Order_ID, Order_Status, Order_Time, Product_ID, Quantity, Total_Price, and User_ID. The combination of Order_ID and User_ID forms the primary key, ensuring entity integrity. The Order_ID and Product_ID, as well as User_ID, are foreign keys referencing the Order, Product, and User tables respectively.\nFinally, the Order_and_Product table is another junction table that links orders and products. It includes columns for Order_ID, Order_Status, Order_Time, Product_ID, Quantity, Total_Price, and User_ID. The combination of Order_ID and Product_ID forms the primary key, ensuring entity integrity. The Order_ID and Product_ID, as well as User_ID, are foreign keys referencing the Order, Product, and User tables respectively. This schema provides a robust and normalized structure for managing user and product data, with constraints to ensure data integrity and consistency.",
  "gold_question": "Shopping Cart System Requirements: Based on the example of JD.com’s shopping cart, the system needs to implement the following functions:\n1.User Functions: Users can log in via multiple methods. Each user has a unique user ID, username, password, contact information, and registration time.\n2.Product Management: Each product includes a product ID, product name, price, stock quantity, and product description.\n3.Order Management: Each order includes an order ID, user ID, product ID, quantity, total price, order time, and order status.\n4.Purchase Management: Each user can add multiple products to the shopping cart and place multiple orders. Each order can contain multiple products.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0438.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0438\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `add_to_cart` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `is_selected` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `add_to_cart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `add_to_cart_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_and_order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`, `user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_order_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_and_product` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_and_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_and_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_and_product_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
